ransactions from both net budget receipts and budget expenditures, to accord with the new reporting procedure outlined in the President's Budget message of January 13, 1960, (see pages 2 and 5). Formerly such transactions were included in the intra-governmental transactions which were deducted in deriving receipts from and payments to the public.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [49, 336, 756, 373], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"2/ Treated as noncash refund deductions from receipts when issued and as cash refund deductions when redeemed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 373, 751, 395], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"3/ Consists of seigniorage and the increment resulting from reduction in the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [821, 198, 1439, 261], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"weight of the gold dollar; excluded from receipts from the public but included in cash deposits in the Treasurer's account. 4/ Figures in this column differ from those published prior to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [820, 259, 1424, 345], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"the September 1960 Treasury Bulletin because a few additional items of budget receipts which are also budget expenditures are included in the interfund transactions deducted from budget receipts and budget expenditures (see footnote 1).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [815, 343, 1000, 376], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"p Preliminary.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [665, 457, 943, 485], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 4\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 481, 780, 679], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"1/ See footnote 1 to Table 3.\\n2/ Net operating expenditures, or receipts (-), as measured by funds provided by or applied to net security transactions reflected in Treasury reports (see Table 7). To a large extent, these Government-sponsored enterprises secure funds for their operations by direct borrowing from the public or by cashing Federal securities which they hold, and they apply the net income received from operations to repayment of borrowing from the public or to investment in Federal securities. On that basis, net expenditures for operations are shown in this table in terms of the combined net of disinvestment in Federal securities and sale of agency obligations in the market, and net\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [821, 488, 1434, 545], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"receipts from operations are shown in terms of the combined net of investment in Federal securities and redemption of agency obligations in the market.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 545, 1111, 630], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"3/ See footnote 4 to Table 3.\\n4/ Not reported prior to 1954.\\n5/ See footnote 1 to Table 7.\\n6/ Does not include revolving securities amounting to $1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 628, 1428, 655], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"p Preliminary.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [692, 738, 976, 769], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 5\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [49, 775, 777, 942], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"1/ Includes reimbursement by Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund and Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund for administrative expenses, and beginning with 1959 for refunds of taxes (treated as an offset to refunda rather than being credited to receipts); reimbursement by Highway Trust Fund for refunds of taxes; reimbursement by the District of Columbia; payment of dividends, interest, etc.; by Federal National Mortgage Association's secondary market operations; and Federal intermediate credit bank franchise tax and repayment of capital stock to the Treasury after December 1956 and before January 1959.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 940, 770, 1002], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"2/ Consists of payment of franchise tax by banks for cooperatives beginning 1955, and also by Federal intermediate credit banks beginning January 1959. 3/ Includes relatively small amounts of deductions from salaries paid by trust\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 1002, 761, 1070], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"funds and Government-sponsored enterprises. Beginning with fiscal year 1958 excludes deductions from salaries of District of Columbia employees (see footnote 5), and beginning with fiscal year 1959 excludes voluntary contributions.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1067, 756, 1122], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"4/ Consists of payments to employees' retirement funds representing United States and Government corporation shares of contributions; payments to the Railroad Retirement Account (for creditable military service), the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 773, 1426, 863], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Unemployment Trust Fund, veterans' life insurance funds, Judicial Survivors Annuity Fund, trust fund for technical services and other assistance under the agricultural conservation program, and District of Columbia; and awards of Indian Claims Commission.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 865, 1454, 1028], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Includes payment by District of Columbia to the Civil Service retirement fund for its share of contributions, and beginning with 1958 also deductions from its payroll; financial adjustments among Railroad Retirement Account, Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance Trust Fund, Federal Disability Insurance Trust Fund, and Unemployment Trust Fund; transfers from Civil Service retirement fund to Foreign Service retirement fund from 1955 through 1957; and transfers from Railroad Unemployment Insurance Administration Fund to Unemployment Trust Fund through 1955.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1028, 1456, 1116], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Figures in this column differ from those previously published because budget receipts which are also budget expenditures are no longer included; see tables 3 and 4.\\n* Less than $500,000.\\np Preliminary.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [698, 1182, 979, 1212], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 6\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 1215, 756, 1252], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"1/ Accrued discount on savings bonds and bills less interest paid on savings\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [49, 1256, 779, 1360], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"2/ Public debt interest due and accrued beginning June 30, 1955, effective date of the change in accounting and reporting from a due and payable basis to an accrual basis; for 1954, consists only of public debt interest checks and coupons outstanding; net increase, or decrease (-). Not reported as a separate clearing account prior to 1954.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1357, 782, 1397], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"3/ Treated as noncash expenditures at the time of issuance of the securities and as cash expenditures at the time of their redemption; net issuance, or\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 27, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1395, 785, 1443], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"4/ Issued in 1936 in exchange for adjusted service certificates held by veterans of World War I. The bonds matured in 1945.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 28, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 1441, 736, 1480], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"5/ Issued in 1947 in payment for accumulated leave. The last of these bonds matured in 1951.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 29, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1217, 1449, 1382], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Part of the United States subscription to the capital of the International Monetary Fund was paid in the form of noninterest-bearing nonnegotiable notes payable on demand (see 1947 Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury, pages 28, 350, and 385). In June 1959 $1,031 million of notes were issued as part of the additional United States subscription to the Fund authorized by an act approved June 17, 1959 (see \\\"Budget Receipts and Expenditures,\\\" Table 4, footnote 10).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 30, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1382, 1444, 1434], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"other accounts; net increase, or decrease (-). For 1953 includes also public debt interest due and unpaid (see footnote 2).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 31, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [818, 1430, 1005, 1465], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"p Preliminary.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 32, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [703, 1542, 978, 1573], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 7\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 33, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1581, 787, 1693], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"In this table, beginning 1954, in accordance with treatment in Budget documents, net investment in United States securities by Government-sponsored enterprises includes a small amount by other enterprises regarded as representing net transactions with the public. In Table 4 under \\\"Trust Account and Other Transactions,\\\" these amounts are included in trust and deposit fund account investment.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 34, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [53, 1689, 770, 1746], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Does not include investments representing acquired securities amounting to $1,643,070 (par value) and donation of securities amounting to $45,800 (par value).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 35, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 1744, 769, 1805], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"3. Accrued discount on savings bonds and bills, which is included in the principal of the public debt, less interest paid on savings bonds and bills redeemed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 36, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [830, 1579, 1429, 1636], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Treated as noncash transactions at the time of issuance and as cash transactions at the time of redemption; net issuance, or redemption (-).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 37, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1634, 1438, 1687], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"5/ Excluded from borrowing because the transactions are treated as expenditures in Table 6.\\nb/ Excluded from borrowing because the transactions are treated as\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 38, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 1685, 1444, 1722], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"7/ Market transactions in public debt securities and agency obliga-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 39, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1720, 1046, 1781], \"page_id\": 32}], \"content\": \"Less than $500,000. Preliminary.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 40, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [6, 37, 204, 70], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"October 1960\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1364, 48, 1393, 70], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"19\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [415, 108, 978, 130], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"ACCOUNT OF THE TREASURER OF THE UNITED STATES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [243, 169, 1113, 202], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"Source and Availability of the Balance in the Treasurer's Account\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 209, 662, 308], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"The account of the Treasurer of the United States reflects not only budget receipts and expenditures but also trust, deposit fund, and public debt transactions.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 327, 653, 503], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"The working cash of the Treasury is held mainly in Treasurer's accounts with Federal Reserve Banks and branches. As the balances in these accounts become depleted, they are restored by calling in (transferring) funds from the tax and loan accounts with thousands of commercial banks throughout the country.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2, 525, 654, 714], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"Deposits to tax and loan accounts occur in the normal course of business under a uniform procedure applicable to all banks whereby customers of banks deposit with them tax payments and funds for the purchase of Government securities. In most cases the transaction involves merely the transfer of money from a customer's\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [730, 206, 1398, 387], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"account to the tax and loan account in the same bank. On occasions, to the extent authorized by the Treasury, banks are permitted to deposit in these accounts proceeds from subscriptions to public debt securities entered for their own account as well as for the account of their customers.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [724, 411, 1402, 591], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"The tax and loan account system permits the Treasury to leave funds in banks and in the communities in which they arise until such time as the Treasury needs the funds for its operations. In this way the Treasury is able to neutralize the effect of its fluctuating operations on bank reserves and the economy.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [734, 615, 1396, 705], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"A detailed description of the Treasury's depositary system may be found in the Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury for 1955, pages 275-284.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [238, 760, 1161, 793], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"Table 1.- Status of the Account of the Treasurer of the United States\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [586, 793, 811, 824], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2, 824, 1393, 1500], \"page_id\": 33}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">End of fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Treasury operating balance</th><th colspan=\\\"5\\\">Assets</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Liabilities 1/</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Balance in account of Treasurer of U. S.</th></tr><tr><th>Available funds in Federal Reserve Banks</th><th>Tax and loan accounts in special depositaries</th><th>Gold in Treasury fund</th><th>Total operating balance</th><th>Silver, coin, and currency</th><th>Unclassified collections, etc.</th><th>In