 old-age insurance taxes and later extended to railroad retirement taxes and many excises, these taxes are paid currently into Treasury depositories and the depositary receipts, as evidence of such payments, are attached to quarterly returns to the Internal Revenue Service.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [789, 1333, 1467, 1819], \"page_id\": 74}], \"content\": \"Under this procedure, the payments are included in budget receipts in the month in which the depository receipts are issued to the taxpayers. Revised accounting procedures effective July 1, 1954, extended the same practice to Internal Revenue Service collection reports.\\n2/ Monthly and fiscal year 1960 figures include social security tax on self-employment income, which is levied and collected as part of the individual income tax. Prior fiscal year figures exclude this tax, on the basis of estimates (see footnote 3), and it is included under \\\"Old-age and disability insurance.\\\"\\n2/ In Internal Revenue Service reports current collections are not separated as to type of tax; the breakdown shown for fiscal years is based on estimates made in accordance with provisions of Sec. 201 of the Social Security Act, as amended (42 U.S.C. 401), for transfer of tax receipts to the trust funds (see \\\"Budget Receipts and Expenditures,\\\" Table 1).\\n4/ Beginning with the fiscal year 1955, collections shown include undelivered depository receipts and unapplied collections. For excise taxes these receipts are included in the total only. Total collection include \\\"Taxes not otherwise classified.\\\"\\n2/ Budget receipts for 1956 were reduced by $3,566 thousand representing tax collections transferred to the Government of Guam pursuant to the act approved August 1, 1950 (48 U.S.C. 1421 h), but this amount was included in collections reported by the Internal Revenue Service. Beginning with 1957, such collections are excluded also in Internal Revenue Service reports.\\n6/ Detail is reported by quarters beginning with the fiscal year 1956.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 13, 214, 57], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"October 1960\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1355, 22, 1394, 59], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"61\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [508, 77, 873, 119], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"INTERNAL REVENUE COLLECTIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [288, 152, 1114, 193], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"INTERNAL REVENUE COLLECTIONS BY PRINCIPAL SOURCES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [79, 189, 1312, 1740], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [257, 1757, 1147, 1801], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"*Beginning with the fiscal year 1955, includes undistributed depository receipts and unapplied collections. The whole amount of such receipts for excise taxes is included under \\\"Other excise taxes.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [83, 1819, 301, 1841], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"Office of the Secretary of the Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1231, 1816, 1302, 1838], \"page_id\": 75}], \"content\": \"8-165-0-1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [56, 31, 82, 51], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"62\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1208, 24, 1439, 64], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [629, 88, 867, 108], \"page_