tes (GBP = 1 USD) - I need to think about this differently\n# Let me get the correct annual average USD per GBP for historical rates\n\n# During the Bretton Woods period, exchange rates were fixed or semi-fixed:\n# Pre-1949: Around $4.03 (actually $4.03 was the pre-war rate from 1934)\n# Sept 1949 Devaluation: $2.80 per GBP and stayed there through 1964\n\n# However, for \"average exchange rate for each respective year\" we need yearly averages\n# Let me check what the IMF or historical records show\n\n# According to historical data from the IMF and other sources:\n# 1948: $4.03 USD/GBP (this was the rate from 1934-1949)\n# 1949: Due to September 1949 devaluation, average would be between $4.03 and $2.80 \n#       = approximately $3.50 (roughly 9 months at $4.03 and 3 months at $2.80)\n# 1950-1964: $2.80 USD/GBP (after devaluation, stable rate)\n\n# More precisely, let me use:\nexchange_rates_usd_per_gbp = {\n    1948: 4.03,   # Pre-devaluation rate\n    1949: 3.50,   # Approximate average (9 months at 4.03, 3 months at 2.80)\n    1950: 2.80,   # Post-devaluation rate\n    1951: 2.80,\n    1952: 2.80,\n    1953: 2.80,\n    1954: 2.80,\n    1955: 2.80,\n    1956: 2.80,\n    1957: 2.80,\n    1958: 2.80,\n    1959: 2.80,\n    1960: 2.80,\n    1961: 2.80,\n    1962: 2.80,\n    1963: 2.80,\n    1964: 2.80,\n}\n\n# Convert to GBP per USD (for dividing USD amounts)\ngbp_per_usd = {year: 1/rate for year, rate in exchange_rates_usd_per_gbp.items()}\n\nfor year in sorted(gbp_per_usd.keys()):\n    print(f\"{year}: {exchange_rates_usd_per_gbp[year]} USD/GBP = {gbp_per_usd[year]:.6f} GBP/USD\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
